============================== ROOT-CAUSE ANALYSIS: test-prop1-no-model-literal.sh FAIL ==============================
File: skills/profitable-article-writer/tests/test-prop1-no-model-literal.sh, lines 20-26:

  20  ok "$([ $rc -eq 0 ] && echo 1 || echo 0)" "PROP-1 dynamic: a real wake completes (rc=$rc): $OUT"
  21  draft="$(grep -oE '^draft_path: .*' "$T/STATE.md" 2>/dev/null | sed 's/^draft_path: //')"
  22  ok "$([ -n "$draft" ] && [ -f "$draft" ] && echo 1 || echo 0)" "PROP-1 dynamic: wake produced a draft artifact to literal-check"
  23  if [ -n "$draft" ] && [ -f "$draft" ]; then
  24    dhits="$(grep -Ec "$FORBIDDEN" "$draft" 2>/dev/null || echo 0)"
  25    ok "$([ "$dhits" = 0 ] && echo 1 || echo 0)" "PROP-1 dynamic: produced draft contains 0 model/API-key literals"
  26  fi

Only the ok() at line 25 fails; the ok() calls at lines 18, 20, 22 (rc=0 wake completion, draft artifact
exists) all PASS with `bash -x` tracing confirming:
  + ok 1 'PROP-1 dynamic: a real wake completes (rc=0): WAKE_RESULT: DRAFT (rounds_used=1, ...)'
  + ok 1 'PROP-1 dynamic: wake produced a draft artifact to literal-check'
  + ok 0 'PROP-1 dynamic: produced draft contains 0 model/API-key literals'   <- only this one fails

Bug: `grep -Ec PATTERN file` follows standard POSIX/BSD/GNU grep exit-status semantics — exit 0 if >=1
line matched, exit 1 if ZERO lines matched (the -c flag changes the OUTPUT format to a count, it does NOT
change the exit-status convention). So when a draft is CORRECTLY literal-free (the desired, correct
outcome), `grep -Ec` prints "0" to stdout AND returns exit code 1. Because line 24 is
`grep -Ec ... || echo 0`, the nonzero exit triggers the `|| echo 0` fallback, which prints A SECOND "0" to
stdout. The command substitution therefore captures "0\n0" (two lines), never a bare "0". Line 25's
`[ "$dhits" = 0 ]` string-compares a two-line value against the literal "0" and is always false — for ANY
literal-free draft, on ANY POSIX-compliant grep (BSD and GNU alike; verified below on this exact host).

Reproduction, independent of run.sh / draft content (proves this is a shell-idiom bug, not a content bug):
  $ printf 'nothing forbidden here\n' > /tmp/clean.txt
  $ grep -Ec 'ZZZ_NEVER_MATCH' /tmp/clean.txt; echo "rc=$?"
  0
  rc=1
  $ dhits="$(grep -Ec 'ZZZ_NEVER_MATCH' /tmp/clean.txt 2>/dev/null || echo 0)"; printf 'dhits=[%s]\n' "$dhits"
  dhits=[0
  0]
  $ [ "$dhits" = 0 ] && echo MATCH || echo NOMATCH
  NOMATCH

The file's OWN static check (lines 8-9) correctly sidesteps this exact class of bug by using
`|| true` + `[ -z "$hits" ]` (empty-string test) instead of `|| echo 0` + numeric-string equality — so the
static PROP-1 check (0 provider-prefixed literals in the skill tree) passes cleanly and is genuinely
verified. The dynamic dhits check at line 24-25 is the one place in this test file that mixes the
`|| echo <value>` fallback pattern with an exact-string-equality assertion, which is what breaks under
correct (zero-match) output for ANY implementation.

Contrast — a version of the same check with the standard fix (not applied to the test file, shown only to
prove the implementation is correct):
  $ dhits="$(grep -Ec 'ZZZ_NEVER_MATCH' /tmp/clean.txt 2>/dev/null)"; dhits="${dhits:-0}"
  $ printf 'dhits=[%s]\n' "$dhits"; [ "$dhits" = 0 ] && echo MATCH || echo NOMATCH
  dhits=[0]
  MATCH

Per the explicit builder instruction "Do NOT weaken/edit the tests," this test file was left untouched.
The Phase 2b implementation (run.sh's dynamic wake, gates/*.sh, identity/accounts.sh) is verified correct
by: (a) the wake completing rc=0 and producing a real draft artifact (both asserted true by this same test
file), (b) an independent manual grep of the produced draft for the exact FORBIDDEN pattern showing zero
matches, and (c) 8/9 test files passing in full, including the STATIC half of this exact PROP (0
provider-prefixed literals anywhere in the skill tree). This finding is surfaced for the adversary/
orchestrator to decide whether to patch the RED-phase test's line 24 (e.g. `dhits="$(grep -Ec ... 2>/dev/null)"; dhits="${dhits:-0}"`).
============================== END ROOT-CAUSE ANALYSIS ==============================
